---
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description = 'What Tokyo After Dark collects, and what it does not.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description={description}>
  <article class="wrap-narrow prose">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated 13 October 2026.</p>
    <p>
      Tokyo After Dark is a static website. It is hosted on GitHub Pages. There is no account system
      and no comment box.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It does not run analytics.</li>
      <li>It does not set its own advertising or tracking cookies. Ads are not switched on.</li>
      <li>
        The newsletter form is a placeholder. It does not send your address to an email service, and
        this site does not store it. With JavaScript on, the form stops before anything is submitted.
        With JavaScript off, the form opens a confirmation page and the address is not included,
        because the email field has no name that would put it in the page address.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, that message is ordinary email
      between you and the editor. The address on this page is a placeholder until it is replaced.
    </p>
    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Posts may link to Google Maps, and later to a booking or affiliate site. Those sites have their
      own policies. See the <a href={url('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a> before using
      a labeled booking link.
    </p>
    <h2>Pages and the host</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub Pages serves the files. GitHub may keep standard server logs for the host. This site does
      not add a tracker on top of that.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a published note is wrong, or you want a personal detail removed, email the address above.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
